#!/usr/bin/env python3

# kg_next — deterministically pick the next problem from the technique graph
# and draw its full input tree (the problem's moves + every transitive
# prerequisite) inline in the terminal.
#
#   utils/kg/kg_next              # pick, print preflight table, draw status+emoji tree
#   utils/kg/kg_next --graph      # same, with node labels (the map)
#   utils/kg/kg_next --no-show    # same, without the drawing
#   utils/kg/kg_next --prepare    # same, then run `make prepare` on the pick
#   make next graph            # makefile form of --graph (make eats dashed args)
#   make next sql              # --group sql: rules 1-3 over one curated group only
#                              # (any group name works: trees, graphs, sql, ...)
#   make next sql assisted     # --assisted: only drills whose latest rep was
#                              # assisted - the unaided rep each is waiting for
#   make next sql cram early   # --early: review the whole group ahead of the
#                              # curve - every node gets its next drill, prereqs
#                              # before dependents regardless of status;
#                              # today's plan is skipped
#   make next prepare          # makefile form of --prepare (the prepare
#                              # target steps aside when next is the goal)
#   KG_NO_PLAN=1 make next     # skip today's frozen study plan (data/study_plan/)
#                              # entirely: no freezing, no plan items - rules
#                              # -1..4 only
#
# Picking rules (same preference order the /next coach uses):
#   -1. session start (fewer than 2 solves since Manila midnight): the
#       gentlest all-SOLID easy (tiny walk, high acceptance) that has not
#       been solved inside WARMUP_COOLDOWN_DAYS — juice, not a rerun of
#       Thursday. Normal rules resume from the day's second solve onward.
#   0. sleep (`<num>-slept` branches, written by `make sleep`): a parked
#      problem is excluded everywhere until the operator runs `make wake` —
#      nothing auto-wakes — and its walk's rusty moves/prereqs get warmed
#      first, via other carriers (rule 0a fires only for a problem woken
#      mid-run, which manual wake makes moot; it is kept for that path)
#   0b. park full (kg_lib.MAX_ASLEEP problems asleep): review is served as
#      usual, new ground is not. A pick that is new ground (rule 3, 4, 5, 6
#      or a plan item that is) is withheld and the parked list is printed
#      with the three ways out: keep going, learn it (notes say "learning",
#      make solved), or fail it (make failed). The cap is the only pressure
#      on a park; without this rule it only showed when make sleep refused
#      a fifth (2026-09-01, four asleep and make next said nothing)
#   0c. ownership rep: a held target's prereq that is SOLID only through
#       assisted reps (kg_lib.owned is False) is never itself FRAGILE/STALE/
#       MISSING, so rules 1-3 would never serve the unaided rep that clears
#       the cross-bank hold (kg_lib.drill_held) - a deadlock, 18 nodes deep on
#       2026-08-29. Serve that prereq's drill first.
#   1. consolidate the FRAGILE node with the highest unlock count (bank
#      problems blocked only by it; oldest evidence breaks ties), via the
#      freshest READY carrier
#   2. spaced re-solve of the STALE node's latest carrier, same unlock-count
#      order — unless the
#      move is DEEP stale (no clean solve within 2x the solid window): then the
#      memory is effectively gone, so re-enter on a gentle fresh carrier the way
#      FRAGILE does, instead of a cold "re-solve" that plays like a new problem
#   3. one new MISSING move whose prereqs are all SOLID — the one that
#      unlocks the most bank problems first
#   3b. frontier mover (PLAN.md phase 4), inside rules 1-3: a due node the
#      bank cannot carry AT ALL (a mapped carrier that is merely warm,
#      asleep, or spent today is waited for, never routed around) promotes
#      a drafted carrier — an unmapped easy/medium
#      from graph/predicted.json whose predicted walk has the target as its
#      only non-solid move and no missing-move flags. Ranked cheap-regime
#      first (kg_lib.predicted_carrier: rarest supporting move's carrier
#      mass, capped at the ~30-problem connectivity threshold), then
#      gentleness. The promotion is in-memory; the solve's evidenced walk
#      (kg_extract) is what maps the problem for real. A promoted draft
#      that comes back mapped to some other move is a MISS; after
#      kg_lib.DRAFT_MISSES of them the target stops promoting (the drafts
#      are wrong about how the operator solves) and the dry warning names
#      it — otherwise the mover spins through every draft in the tier.
#   4. nothing rusty and nothing new: a summit — the gentlest unsolved Hard
#      whose whole walk is already SOLID and mature (kg_lib.mature: spaced
#      clean reps + a real-problem carry proof — a badge earned in one burst
#      of drills does not yet carry a Hard).
#      A Hard is never a CARRIER (not where
#      a rusty move gets its rep), but once it is all-green it is exactly what
#      to work on next, so it is picked here rather than behind `make hard`.
# One-new-move rule is enforced: every other move in the walk must be SOLID.
# Drill-success gate (kg_lib.drill_gated): a MISSING/FRAGILE/deep-stale target
# with a drill bank gets ONLY its drill until a clean rep clears the status —
# a struggled drill holds the carrier instead of unlocking it.
#
# Below the pick, one line says how much review stands between now and
# the first pick that is new ground (review_ahead): the picker is replayed
# on a copy of the evidence, every pick granted a clean unaided rep, the
# day advanced when the once-a-day rules leave nothing to serve, until the
# pick is a MISSING move (rule 3) or an all-solid problem (rules 4-6). The
# count is the best case: a struggled rep adds to it.
#
# NOTE: the default drawing writes only status + a random face from that
# status's pool (SOLID 💪, STALE 😐, ...) — no move names — so the tree
# can be used for pattern recognition. --graph names the walk: that is
# the "show me the map" flow. The /next chat flow seals targets.

